    %% CURRENT SCHEMA: WEB APP (generated from the migrations; comments checked on 2026-10-09)
    %% One Supabase database holds two inspection systems:
    %%   WEB    = form_responses, answers, sites_pa, S26_pdf_jobs, and others. Used only by webapp/.
    %%   LEGACY = inspectheader, inspectdetails, and others. Used by FNR/ and
    %%            googleSheets/code.gs. See ER_Diagram_Legacy.mmd.
    %%   SHARED = luperson. The only table that all three clients use.
    %% Data in one system is not visible in the other system.

    %% Rules for this diagram:
    %% - The block between the GENERATED markers is made by `npm run diagrams`
    %%   from webapp/supabase/migrations/*.sql, applied in filename order. It
    %%   shows every table and column that the migrations make, except the
    %%   legacy read models listed at the end. Do not edit that block. Change
    %%   tools/diagrams/src/config.mjs to add a note to a column.
    %% - auth_users is hand-written, because Supabase makes auth.users.
    %% - The production database can have more columns. They are not shown.
    %%   Production gets each migration by hand (see the migration headers).
    %% - Mermaid does not allow spaces or hyphens in names. The quoted comment
    %%   gives the real column name when it is different. UK on one column means
    %%   unique; "unique (a, b)" means the columns are unique together.
    %% - Code that reads and writes these tables: webapp/utils/supabase/queries.ts,
    %%   webapp/utils/form-actions.ts, webapp/utils/steward-actions.ts,
    %%   webapp/utils/kml-import-actions.ts, webapp/app/api/ (for example
    %%   webapp/app/api/profile/route.ts) and webapp/lib/pdf/.
    %% - The web app keys users by auth.users.id. It uses luperson only to check
    %%   if an email belongs to a steward (isSteward in queries.ts). There is no
    %%   foreign key between auth.users and luperson.
    %% - people has one row for each login. The trigger create_person_on_signup
    %%   on auth.users (function create_person_for_new_user) makes it.
    %% - site_stewards.site_id is the primary key, so a site has one steward.
    %% - sites_pa.protected_area_id is an optional link to protected_areas.id.
    %%   The KML import (webapp/utils/kml-import-actions.ts) matches rows on (folder, fid).
    %% - The role is in raw_app_meta_data (app_metadata.role and
    %%   app_metadata.authenticated). The RLS policies read it.

